<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.4: Match Expressions and Tables with Situations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01282</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.4: Match Expressions and Tables with Situations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>34756f8c-77db-4d09-95a8-c3f2105091fd</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title> Activity</title>
<para>Here are verbal descriptions of two situations, followed by tables and expressions that could help answer one of the
  questions in the situations.</para>
<list>
  <item> Situation 1: A person has 80 followers on social media. The number of followers triples each year. How many
    followers will she have after 4 years? </item>
  <item> Situation 2: A tank contains 80 gallons of water and is getting filled at a rate of 3 gallons per minute. How
    many gallons of water will be in the tank after 4 minutes? </item>
</list>
<para>Use the descriptions of Situation 1 and Situation 2 to help you answer questions 1 – 6. Be prepared to explain
  how the table or expression answers the question.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="46091c8a-e6c2-409a-99d0-06178b88c554" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b3abcd5f-9a20-45b8-9a89-cd48fa8ad671" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 1" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which situation best describes \(80 \cdot 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 1 </para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="db6e2c86-ad77-4d31-b026-d09c343446fa" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 1" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which situation best describes the following table? </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>
              80
            </entry>
            <entry>
              240
            </entry>
            <entry>
              720
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2,160
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6,480
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 1. The table shows the growth of the followers multiplied by 3 each year. </para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3d437c94-a607-45ea-87b2-d75018374847" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 2" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which situation best describes \(80+3+3+3+3\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 2 </para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6664cb81-3aa9-44bb-b4c6-2095d8377810" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 2" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which situation best describes \(80+4 \cdot 3\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 2. \(4 \cdot 3\) is another way of expressing \(3+3+3+3\).</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f10b1fd5-6fb0-4c9d-a603-9085bcf49d55" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 2" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which situation best describes the following table? </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
            <entry>
              80
            </entry>
            <entry>
              83
            </entry>
            <entry>
              86
            </entry>
            <entry>
              89
            </entry>
            <entry>
              92
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 2. The table shows the gallons of water in the tank increasing by 3 gallons each minute.
      </para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="446ac711-2e50-418b-9706-849368de01bc" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Situation 1" data-solution-options="[&quot;Situation 1&quot;, &quot;Situation 2&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which situation best describes \(80\cdot 81\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Situation 1. The 81 comes from \(3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3\).</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
